    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d236-f1" n="1" type="source" xml:id="d236-f1-content">
                <p>Source: Central Intelligence Agency, Office of the Director of Central
                    Intelligence, Job 81B00112R: Subject Files, Box 16, Folder 36: (SCC) Nicaragua.
                    Secret. Drafted on June 29. [<hi rendition="#italic">name not declassified</hi>]
                    sent a copy of the memorandum to Turner under a June 29 covering memorandum,
                        [<hi rendition="#italic">text not declassified</hi>]. The meeting took place
                    in the White House Situation Room.</p>
            </note>
            <note corresp="#d236-f2" n="2" xml:id="d236-f2-content">
                <p>In telegram 5865 from Caracas, June 28, Luers reported that he had met with Perez
                    to discuss the situation in Nicaragua. Perez was “not displeased by the
                    mechanism we planned but doubted it would work.” (National Archives, RG 59,
                    Central Foreign Policy File, P840140–1679)</p>
            </note>
            <note corresp="#d236-f3" n="3" xml:id="d236-f3-content">
                <p>See <ref target="#d235">Document 235</ref>.</p>
            </note>
